  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Monday)\nIssued at 1115 AM CDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nSynoptic level weather patterns will begin to change today as a \nshortwave moves northwest of the forecast area. This feature will \nbe strong enough to push the ridge, currently centered over the \nlower Mississippi Valley, eastward. At the surface, weather \nconditions will not change much through the end of the week minus \na slight increase in dewpoint temperatures. Daily highs will be in\nthe mid 70s and lower 80s with morning lows in the 40s and 50s. \nFire weather concerns will slowly be alleviated thanks to the \nincrease in moisture. However, the prolonged dry spell in \ncombination with dry fuels will keep burn bans in place. Adhere to\nlocal burning guidelines and dispose of cigarettes properly.\n\nBy Saturday, an upper level low will form over Texas. This feature\nwill advect increased moisture into the Mid-South, allowing rain\nchances to return by Saturday morning. The latest guidance paints\na rainy Halloween with showers lasting through Sunday evening. The\nprobability of rainfall totals exceeding one inch Saturday and\nSunday has increased to 40 percent over northeast Mississippi.\nAdditional rain chances will manifest early next week as a bowling\nball trough develops over central CONUS. It remains too early to\ntell specifics, but we will be watching the evolution of this\nfeature as we get closer to the event.",
